===Etymology 1===
{{root|en|ine-pro|*gʰerdʰ-}}
From {{inh|en|enm|girden}}, {{m|enm|gerden}}, {{m|enm|gurden|gürden}}, from {{inh|en|ang|gyrdan||to put a belt around, to put a girdle around}}, from {{inh|en|gem-pro|*gurdijaną|t=to gird}}, from {{der|en|ine-pro|*gʰerdʰ-}}. Cognate with {{cog|fy|gurdzje}}, {{m|fy|girdzje}}, {{cog|nl|gorden}}, {{cog|de|gürten}}, {{cog|sv|gjorda}}, {{cog|is|gyrða}}, {{cog|sq|ngërthej||to tie together by weaving, to bind}}.

====Verb====
{{en-verb|past2=girt}}

# {{lb|en|transitive}} To [[bind]] with a [[flexible]] [[rope]] or [[cord]].
#: {{ux|en|The fasces were '''girt''' about with twine in bundles large.}}
#* {{RQ:Shakespeare Henry 6-2|act=I|scene=i|page=120|column=2|passage=We heere create thee the firſt Duke of Suffolke, / And '''girt''' thee with the Sword. Coſin of Yorke}}
#* {{RQ:KJV|Psalms|45|3|passage='''Gird''' thy sword vpon thy thigh, O most mightie: with thy glory and thy maiestie.}}
# {{lb|en|transitive}} To [[encircle]] with, or as if with a [[belt]].
#: {{ux|en|The lady '''girt''' herself with silver chain, from which she hung a golden shear.}}
#* {{RQ:KJV|Leviticus|8|7|passage=And he put vpon him the coate, and '''girded''' him with the girdle, and clothed him with the robe, and put the Ephod vpon him, and he '''girded''' him with the curious girdle of the Ephod, and bound it vnto him therewith.}}
#* {{quote-song|en|year=1878|author=w:Peter Dodds McCormick|passage=Australia's sons, let us rejoice, / For we are young and free /  We've golden soil and wealth for toil / Our home is '''girt''' by sea|title=w:Advance Australia Fair}}
#* {{RQ:Haggard She|passage=It took me back across the dim gulf of ages to some happy home in dead Imperial Kôr, where this winsome lady '''girt''' about with beauty had lived and died, and dying taken her last-born with her to the tomb.}}
# {{lb|en|transitive|reflexive}} To [[prepare]] (oneself) for an [[action]].
#* {{RQ:KJV|Isaiah|8|9|passage=Associate your selues, O ye people, and yee shalbe broken in pieces; and giue eare all ye of farre countreys: '''gird''' your selues, and ye shalbe broken in pieces; '''gird''' your selues, and ye shalbe broken in pieces.}}
#* {{quote-web|en|url=http://www.theguardian.com/theguardian/2000/apr/15/weekend7.weekend8|title=The net addict|date=2000-04-15|author=Tanya Millbank|work=The Guardian|passage={{...}} I was intrigued by the notion of ‘virtual beating’, so I entered the words in the Mamma search engine. I '''girded''' myself for the sleaziest sites on the net, the kind that advertise the video of Pamela Anderson and Tommy Lee uncut, {{...|but to my surprise what I got instead was The Church Of Sarah Michelle Gellar, Save Souls and Virtual Jerusalem.com, offering the Torah channel.}}}}
#* {{quote-web|en|url=https://www.theguardian.com/world/2022/dec/09/putin-shelling-ukraine-power-grid-russia-president-strikes-energy-infrastructure|title=Putin suggests possibility of settlement to end war in Ukraine|author=Andrew Roth|date=2022-12-09|work=The Guardian|passage=The remarks came just days after Putin appeared to be '''girding''' Russians for a protracted war in Ukraine, saying that his military operation could be a “long-term process”.}}

